  "markdown_report": "**Insights and directions.** (1) The starting gate can condition residual updates on recent behavior while preserving NextItNet’s identity shortcuts; this targets outdated-interest carryover. (2) Causal summaries must exclude padding and future items, preserving next-item supervision. (3) A gate alone does not resolve the observed ranking gap: CDs has sampled-negative margin 12.03 but diagnostic catalog HR@10 of zero.\n\nRelated work suggests three directions. (1) [NextItNet](https://arxiv.org/abs/1808.05163) supports retaining causal residual convolutions. (2) [Scalable Cross-Entropy](https://dspace.mit.edu/entities/publication/5392aca9-0bae-4176-9b3a-a8165957ba26) motivates informative competitors, without establishing gains here. (3) [UFNRec](https://arxiv.org/abs/2208.04116) motivates caution because unobserved items can be false negatives. Consequently, stronger recent-item weighting and harder negatives remain hypotheses, particularly given small deletion samples and position-shift confounding.\n\n**Framework and candidates.** The design space crosses representation conditioning (recent summary), discrimination (candidate competition), and evidence enrichment (permitted item text). All candidates retain one jointly trained NextItNet per category.\n\nScores below use O=originality, P=potential, U=user alignment, M=model alignment, D=implementation difficulty; higher D means harder. Each entry includes a benefit (+) and limitation (−).\n\n| Idea | O | P | U | M | D |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Recent-summary residual gate | 4: +context adaptation; −familiar gating | 7: +adaptive intent; −recency varies | 8: +current priority; −no compatibility evidence | 5: +tests temporal use; −order already matters | 3: +small layer; −causal masking |\n| Mixed-negative softmax on the gated backbone | 4: +targeted combination; −established objective | 8: +ranking focus; −false negatives | 8: +specific alternatives; −intent implicit | 9: +addresses margin/catalog gap; −training evidence only | 4: +shared scorer; −sampling exclusions |\n| Scratch-trained title/description embedding addition | 5: +permitted semantics; −known fusion | 7: +content grounding; −sparse text | 8: +style/task clues; −compatibility uncertain | 6: +richer discrimination; −diagnosis indirect | 6: +simple pooling; −text pipeline |\n\n**Selected experiment: mixed-negative softmax on the recent-gated NextItNet.** At 10% progress, change the training objective while retaining the proposed gate. This targets two user failures: older purchases dominating current priorities through recent conditioning, and broad matches outranking specific choices through competition against stronger alternatives. Its measured motivation is positive sampled margins coexisting with poor catalog ranking, rather than an asserted lack of order sensitivity.\n\n```python\nr = causal_masked_recent_mean(item_embeddings, window=5)\nfor block in nextitnet_blocks:\n    h = mask * (h + sigmoid(block.gate(r)) * block.residual_update(h))\n# Start with uniform multi-negative training; ramp moderate mining later.\npool = unique_uniform_training_eligible_items()\nneg = mix_random_and_moderately_high_scoring(pool, h.detach())\nloss = cross_entropy(scores(h, [positive, *neg]), target=0)\n```\n\nKeep the uniform baseline loss as the first comparison; proposed mining proportions are experimental. Exclude padding, target, and prefix-observed training items, without consulting future labels. Preserve final-nonpadding readout, diagnostic APIs, matching predictor construction, all four routes, fixed seeds, 200 epochs maximum, and 200 batches/epoch. Select exclusively by pinned macro validation HR@10; no gains are claimed.",
  "idea": {
    "description": "Train the proposed recent-summary-gated corrected NextItNet with multi-negative softmax and a gradual mixture of uniform and moderately hard negatives. Each category uses one jointly trained network and one selected checkpoint.",
    "motivation": "Recent conditioning targets outdated-interest carryover; stronger candidate competition targets broad matches outranking specific alternatives. Quantitatively, strong sampled-negative margins coexist with low full-catalog training-prefix HR@10, motivating improved discrimination without treating diagnostics as validation estimates.",
    "implementation_notes": "First compare uniform multi-negative softmax against the supplied objective, then assess gradual moderate mining within the shared budget. An initial proposal is 32 negatives, with the mined fraction ramping from zero to 25%; these are unvalidated settings. Mine from a deduplicated uniform pool using detached current-model scores; retain moderately high-scoring candidates rather than only extremes. Exclude padding, the current target, and prefix-observed training items; never use later validation/test interactions for exclusions. Do not apply a uniform LogQ correction to deterministically mined candidates. Compute the gate summary from masked item embeddings over at most five preceding/current input positions, never the shifted target. Gate only the complete residual update, preserving the identity shortcut. Preserve ModelView interfaces and DiagnosisProbe/diagnosis_interpreter_prompt contracts; include summary dependencies in architecture probes. Remask after final normalization and gather the maximum nonpadding index, handling empty histories explicitly. Synchronize the architecture in the predictor writer and checkpoint configuration. Retain Movies_and_TV, Industrial_and_Scientific, Electronics, and CDs_and_Vinyl routing; DATA_DIR = os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR']; trial-local artifacts; preprocessing seed 0; training seed 42; maximum 200 epochs; exactly 200 batches per epoch; single-GPU execution. No checkpoint averaging, independent auxiliary scorers, pretrained weights, or unavailable metadata. Baseline source was not supplied in this prompt, so this specifies an integration experiment rather than a verified runnable replacement.",
    "pseudocode": "r = causal_masked_recent_mean(item_emb(sequence), window=5)\nh = baseline_input_features(sequence)\nfor block in corrected_nextitnet_blocks:\n    update = block.complete_residual_update(h)\n    h = nonpadding_mask * (h + sigmoid(block.gate(r)) * update)\nfeatures = final_norm(h) * nonpadding_mask\nfor valid training position:\n    pool = sample_unique_uniform_candidates_excluding_padding_target_and_prefix_history()\n    with no_grad():\n        hardness = predict_score(features.detach(), pool)\n    negatives = choose_random_plus_moderately_hard(pool, hardness, scheduled_fraction)\n    loss += cross_entropy(predict_score(features, concat(positive, negatives)), target=0)\noptimize_one_network(loss)\n# Inference: gather final nonpadding feature; score with this same network.\n# Host selection: fixed four-category macro validation HR@10.",
    "originality": {
      "score": 4,
      "positive": "Connects recent-conditioned residual updates with candidate competition motivated by the supplied diagnoses.",
      "negative": "Gating and multi-negative softmax are established techniques; novelty is primarily the constrained combination."
    },
    "future_potential": {
      "score": 8,
      "positive": "Creates a tractable investigation of temporal conditioning and ranking discrimination within causal convolution models.",
      "negative": "False negatives and category-dependent recency could erase benefits; benchmark improvements remain unmeasured."
    },
    "code_difficulty": {
      "score": 4,
      "positive": "Reuses the existing convolution backbone, embeddings, and scorer with a small gate and revised candidate loss.",
      "negative": "Requires careful causal masking, candidate exclusions, budget control, and synchronized training/predictor definitions."
    }
  },
